==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*hlaibha-'', from Indo-European ''*kel-, *klei-''.  Cognate with Old High German ''[[hleib]]'' (German ''[[Laib]]''), Old Norse ''[[hleifr]]'' (Old Swedish ''lēver''), Gothic [[𐌷𐌻𐌰𐌹𐍆𐍃]].  The IE root is also the source of Ancient Greek '''{{polytonic|[[κλίβανος]]}}''' ‘baking oven’, Old Slavic ''chlěb’'' (Russian ''[[хлеб]]'' ‘bread’).

